(4256950, 611770, 68504, '<td valign="top">Is it dead?<br/>Edit:  I know this is a rude and crude comment;  also that every care was taken with the infant, and that slings have been the carrier of choice ever since the stork. Perhaps it is a tribute to your skill that I was so viscerally affected, and also a recognition, I believe, of the power of an image.  It was the bunching towards being closed at the top that reminded me of the way turkeys are packaged, and all at once the baby became a thing, and then, for me, a line was crossed.  <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-19 15:37:34.</i></td>', 'Is it dead?Edit:  I know this is a rude and crude comment;  also that every care was taken with the infant, and that slings have been the carrier of choice ever since the stork. Perhaps it is a tribute to your skill that I was so viscerally affected, and also a recognition, I believe, of the power of an image.  It was the bunching towards being closed at the top that reminded me of the way turkeys are packaged, and all at once the baby became a thing, and then, for me, a line was crossed.  ', '2007-11-19 02:04:37.000000', '2007-11-19 15:37:34.000000', 0),
