(4257156, 611737, 30982, '<td valign="top">When you get a dSLR (rumor has it you will) and if you get a chance, go reshoot this.  Find a ledge or something to set the camera on, and use the self-timer.  Set the aperture to about f/7.1 or so in Aperture Priority mode (you have downloaded and are reading the manual, right?) and see what it tells you as a shutter speed.  Now set the camera to manual mode, leave the aperture at f/7.1, but set the shutter speed a stop faster than it told you.  Take a shot.  Now change the aperture to one stop smaller and take it again.  When shooting at night (and I learned this from SandyP), underexpose by a stop or two.</td>', 'When you get a dSLR (rumor has it you will) and if you get a chance, go reshoot this.  Find a ledge or something to set the camera on, and use the self-timer.  Set the aperture to about f/7.1 or so in Aperture Priority mode (you have downloaded and are reading the manual, right?) and see what it tells you as a shutter speed.  Now set the camera to manual mode, leave the aperture at f/7.1, but set the shutter speed a stop faster than it told you.  Take a shot.  Now change the aperture to one stop smaller and take it again.  When shooting at night (and I learned this from SandyP), underexpose by a stop or two.', '2007-11-19 04:42:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4257157, 610882, 34938, '<td valign="top">underrated to the max</td>', 'underrated to the max', '2007-11-19 04:42:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4257159, 611556, 30982, '<td valign="top">I guess it''s just me, but I kinda like the harsh light and the shadow.  You could clone out the shadow (or just paint it out with white) and try Ed''s suggestion of really cranking the contrast to get his face even whiter.</td>', 'I guess it''s just me, but I kinda like the harsh light and the shadow.  You could clone out the shadow (or just paint it out with white) and try Ed''s suggestion of really cranking the contrast to get his face even whiter.', '2007-11-19 04:43:56.000000', NULL, 0),
