(4265933, 610641, 61651, '<td valign="top">Very evocative and striking.  Definitely underrated.</td>', 'Very evocative and striking.  Definitely underrated.', '2007-11-23 15:10:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4265999, 611020, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>You have done some things very well here.  She looks comfortable in her pose and her make up and hair is absolutely fabulous.  I like the natural light, but for this pose, it lights "too much."  I think some sidelighting, or even backlighting might help it to be more dramatic.  If you want to keep the natural light, i would suggest a closer crop so that just her face is showing.  <br/> <br/>Several people commented on her size, and I am wondering if the pose you have her in actually makes her look larger than she is.  Straight on, unless you are toothpick sized, will always make you look larger if I am not mistaken.  Perhaps if she were turned slightly and looking back at you it would be more flattering.<br/> <br/>You met the challenge.  The shot is bw, and it is okay.  I think a bit more contrast would help to add interest.  To me, it seems as if there is a dark gray ranging to a lighter gray, but no distinct blacks and whites, and this gives the shot a "flat" feeling.<br/> <br/>The background -- that one item probably dropped your potential score more than anything.  A wrinkled background appears hurried and sloppy.  Either iron it, or take the wrinkles out in post processing.<br/> <br/>Overall, pretty well done.<br/> <br/>If I need to further clarify anything, please let me know.<br/> <br/>karmat</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat You have done some things very well here.  She looks comfortable in her pose and her make up and hair is absolutely fabulous.  I like the natural light, but for this pose, it lights "too much."  I think some sidelighting, or even backlighting might help it to be more dramatic.  If you want to keep the natural light, i would suggest a closer crop so that just her face is showing.   Several people commented on her size, and I am wondering if the pose you have her in actually makes her look larger than she is.  Straight on, unless you are toothpick sized, will always make you look larger if I am not mistaken.  Perhaps if she were turned slightly and looking back at you it would be more flattering. You met the challenge.  The shot is bw, and it is okay.  I think a bit more contrast would help to add interest.  To me, it seems as if there is a dark gray ranging to a lighter gray, but no distinct blacks and whites, and this gives the shot a "flat" feeling. The background -- that one item probably dropped your potential score more than anything.  A wrinkled background appears hurried and sloppy.  Either iron it, or take the wrinkles out in post processing. Overall, pretty well done. If I need to further clarify anything, please let me know. karmat', '2007-11-23 16:00:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4266135, 610760, 61651, '<td valign="top">Beautifully in its simplicity - very nice meets the challenge, too. :)</td>', 'Beautifully in its simplicity - very nice meets the challenge, too. :)', '2007-11-23 18:33:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4266136, 610543, 61651, '<td valign="top">You gave me a good laugh when I first saw this - a dual-purpose duotone. :)  Nice idea for either challenge.</td>', 'You gave me a good laugh when I first saw this - a dual-purpose duotone. :)  Nice idea for either challenge.', '2007-11-23 18:34:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4266150, 609982, 83856, '<td valign="top">Very nice photo.Grey colour is perfect.</td>', 'Very nice photo.Grey colour is perfect.', '2007-11-23 19:03:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4266686, 611698, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi from the critique club</b> <br/> <br/>I am not trying to be unpolite or to bash your photo with my critique.<br/>With checking the box that you wanted a critue you asked for honnesty and that is what I am trying to give. Please dont be offended by my comments, it is all just to try and help you.<br/> <br/>Ok first thing I noticed was the crop, you could have gone more towards the face or get a bit more space between you and the model. The way the crop is now she looks like she is cut in half, and I dont see any pose.<br/>Her arm and hands are not in the photo so I dont see what she is supposed to be doing.<br/>Try to get what you want to "say" into the frame, everything else is clutter :)<br/>So if you tried to capture her attitude and you need the pose for that, then put a few steps back and get the pose in your photo. If it is the expression on the face that you want so show, step in, make a pic of her face.<br/> <br/>2nd thing I noticed was the background. Not your fault as you where on a lighting workshop, but on my monitor I can see even the stiches in the cloth behind her and on the left side I see a big wrinkle.<br/>As this was an advanced editing challenge you could have shopped that out.<br/> <br/>3rd thing I noticed is that it is black and white, and black and white in most voters view is not duotone. It is, but it is not, you know what I mean? If the voters expect duotone, then b/w wont do it for them.<br/> <br/>All in all not a bad picture but it could have been better and I hope I pointed out what I would have done. Believe me, I am only one person and I dont know everything, so see it as it is. I''ts one persons view.<br/> <br/>And as alway''s, if YOU are happy with the photo then it is OK, you cant please everybody.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hi from the critique club  I am not trying to be unpolite or to bash your photo with my critique.With checking the box that you wanted a critue you asked for honnesty and that is what I am trying to give. Please dont be offended by my comments, it is all just to try and help you. Ok first thing I noticed was the crop, you could have gone more towards the face or get a bit more space between you and the model. The way the crop is now she looks like she is cut in half, and I dont see any pose.Her arm and hands are not in the photo so I dont see what she is supposed to be doing.Try to get what you want to "say" into the frame, everything else is clutter :)So if you tried to capture her attitude and you need the pose for that, then put a few steps back and get the pose in your photo. If it is the expression on the face that you want so show, step in, make a pic of her face. 2nd thing I noticed was the background. Not your fault as you where on a lighting workshop, but on my monitor I can see even the stiches in the cloth behind her and on the left side I see a big wrinkle.As this was an advanced editing challenge you could have shopped that out. 3rd thing I noticed is that it is black and white, and black and white in most voters view is not duotone. It is, but it is not, you know what I mean? If the voters expect duotone, then b/w wont do it for them. All in all not a bad picture but it could have been better and I hope I pointed out what I would have done. Believe me, I am only one person and I dont know everything, so see it as it is. I''ts one persons view. And as alway''s, if YOU are happy with the photo then it is OK, you cant please everybody. ', '2007-11-24 04:10:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4266689, 610368, 22781, '<td valign="top"><b>Hi from the critique club</b> <br/> <br/>I am not trying to be unpolite or to bash your photo with my critique.<br/>With checking the box that you wanted a critue you asked for honnesty and that is what I am trying to give. Please dont be offended by my comments, it is all just to try and help you.<br/> <br/>Ok, the 1st thing that I noticed is that it is b/w<br/>I strongly think that voters will expect some other tones then b/w and I think that has lost you some votes.<br/> <br/>2nd this could be a great landscape in color, but these tones dont do the landscape justice I think.<br/> <br/>You have to capture voters with your entry and "hit them in the face with it" make it simple, make it strong, put something in your photo that makes it unique and you will see your votes go up.<br/> <br/>All in all not a bad picture but it could have been better and I hope I pointed out what I would have done. Believe me, I am only one person and I dont know everything, so see it as it is. I''ts one persons view.<br/> <br/>And as alway''s, if YOU are happy with the photo then it is OK, you cant please everybody.</td>', 'Hi from the critique club  I am not trying to be unpolite or to bash your photo with my critique.With checking the box that you wanted a critue you asked for honnesty and that is what I am trying to give. Please dont be offended by my comments, it is all just to try and help you. Ok, the 1st thing that I noticed is that it is b/wI strongly think that voters will expect some other tones then b/w and I think that has lost you some votes. 2nd this could be a great landscape in color, but these tones dont do the landscape justice I think. You have to capture voters with your entry and "hit them in the face with it" make it simple, make it strong, put something in your photo that makes it unique and you will see your votes go up. All in all not a bad picture but it could have been better and I hope I pointed out what I would have done. Believe me, I am only one person and I dont know everything, so see it as it is. I''ts one persons view. And as alway''s, if YOU are happy with the photo then it is OK, you cant please everybody.', '2007-11-24 04:18:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4266814, 611460, 41047, '<td valign="top">wow, lev! congrats again!! you''re on a roll :) this is a stunning capture.</td>', 'wow, lev! congrats again!! you''re on a roll :) this is a stunning capture.', '2007-11-24 09:36:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4266853, 611333, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hello,<br/>    Tho I like the crop the image overall is to centeralized for me.Sometimes it works sometimes not here it did not. Moveing it to the left hand corner &amp; down a bit would have been better here. The blowout on the front &amp; right pedal is a bit distracting, the use of a polerizer would have been a huge help to you here cutting down the glear or eleminating it completely.The color of the rose (pink) seems very flat no pop to it at all. Not sure if it is the blur tool or what but some sections of the image have real nice detail while others do not. From an overall prospective it appears to me that way to much editing was done here on a  subject that really does''nt need it. I do realize that this was an advanced editing challange but we must not forget the photography here. I think you just tried to do to much with to little here.</td>', 'Hello,    Tho I like the crop the image overall is to centeralized for me.Sometimes it works sometimes not here it did not. Moveing it to the left hand corner & down a bit would have been better here. The blowout on the front & right pedal is a bit distracting, the use of a polerizer would have been a huge help to you here cutting down the glear or eleminating it completely.The color of the rose (pink) seems very flat no pop to it at all. Not sure if it is the blur tool or what but some sections of the image have real nice detail while others do not. From an overall prospective it appears to me that way to much editing was done here on a  subject that really does''nt need it. I do realize that this was an advanced editing challange but we must not forget the photography here. I think you just tried to do to much with to little here.', '2007-11-24 10:52:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4266864, 611847, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hi,<br/>  Neat image, I like the way you cropped here brings full attention to the water nicely done. Love the detail you captured here crisp  &amp; sharp. I also like the way you famed it all in here top to bottom, left to right. Your duotones here are a nice soft blend, I like it. The only thing here that is really bothersome is that light. It is a major distraction, moving it left or right showing just the finges of it would have helped greatly. Overall like I said this is a really neat image nice work.</td>', 'Hi,  Neat image, I like the way you cropped here brings full attention to the water nicely done. Love the detail you captured here crisp  & sharp. I also like the way you famed it all in here top to bottom, left to right. Your duotones here are a nice soft blend, I like it. The only thing here that is really bothersome is that light. It is a major distraction, moving it left or right showing just the finges of it would have helped greatly. Overall like I said this is a really neat image nice work.', '2007-11-24 11:07:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4267036, 610325, 85460, '<td valign="top">outstanding! I LOVE the contrast and texture, it''s exceptionally beautiful. Great job!</td>', 'outstanding! I LOVE the contrast and texture, it''s exceptionally beautiful. Great job!', '2007-11-24 13:58:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4267645, 611092, 27133, '<td valign="top">You hit the 6.0 mark....that is good.  Be happy!!</td>', 'You hit the 6.0 mark....that is good.  Be happy!!', '2007-11-25 00:35:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4267719, 609982, 86940, '<td valign="top">This is really dramatic.  I like it. :)</td>', 'This is really dramatic.  I like it. :)', '2007-11-25 02:07:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4267750, 611727, 47483, '<td valign="top">Okey I am going to be little bitch here, I really do not like it very much. For me its a so so photo. <br/>My not liking it may be because of the reason that I am not able to think what you thought about it. Or may be I am not able to feel what you felt. <br/>But seeing that scoring high on DPC is not you wanted to do here. (I have not doubt that you are one wonderful photographer) I feel happy that you are submitting what you like. I truely admire this.<br/> <br/>In this photo the most troubling part is the top of the photo, where the couple is placed too close to top, suggesting a lack of balance. The photo looks unbalanced and bothers the eyes. The larger black border might have helped it.<br/>The processing you have kept it simple and probably that is the soul of this photo. <br/>I wouldn''t call it underrated in fact by DPC standards it has scored more than it might have. <br/></td>', 'Okey I am going to be little bitch here, I really do not like it very much. For me its a so so photo. My not liking it may be because of the reason that I am not able to think what you thought about it. Or may be I am not able to feel what you felt. But seeing that scoring high on DPC is not you wanted to do here. (I have not doubt that you are one wonderful photographer) I feel happy that you are submitting what you like. I truely admire this. In this photo the most troubling part is the top of the photo, where the couple is placed too close to top, suggesting a lack of balance. The photo looks unbalanced and bothers the eyes. The larger black border might have helped it.The processing you have kept it simple and probably that is the soul of this photo. I wouldn''t call it underrated in fact by DPC standards it has scored more than it might have. ', '2007-11-25 02:44:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4267777, 610592, 41337, '<td valign="top">Interesting. You leave a lot to the imagination. The uneven glow gives the orb movement and weight. The bright spot is like a spark in the darkness. This might be what the universe looks like from afar.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-25 08:04:06.</i></td>', 'Interesting. You leave a lot to the imagination. The uneven glow gives the orb movement and weight. The bright spot is like a spark in the darkness. This might be what the universe looks like from afar.', '2007-11-25 05:29:07.000000', '2007-11-25 08:04:06.000000', 0),
(4268534, 611814, 87017, '<td valign="top">Nice placement.<br/>The four corners of the center of the cross, form an x spot on the bridge of her nose.  "Spot on."<br/>_cellar<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-11-25 20:42:18.</i></td>', 'Nice placement.The four corners of the center of the cross, form an x spot on the bridge of her nose.  "Spot on."_cellar', '2007-11-25 20:41:28.000000', '2007-11-25 20:42:18.000000', 0),
(4268936, 610641, 64795, '<td valign="top">There''s no way this didn''t ribbon. Geez.  I''m amazed.</td>', 'There''s no way this didn''t ribbon. Geez.  I''m amazed.', '2007-11-26 01:33:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4268939, 611825, 64795, '<td valign="top">This is marvelous.  Excellent work.</td>', 'This is marvelous.  Excellent work.', '2007-11-26 01:34:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4269298, 611746, 43073, '<td valign="top">The initial feeling here is that I was looking at a child captured, hidden somewhere, a child yearning to get out. But the more I looked, the more I realized that the child is free, and the almost mournful face is the expression that she wears looking in at us, wishing all of us adults, walled in behind our jobs and our fears and our perceptions, walled in by ourselves, could see animals in the clouds again, or run just to run, or slide down a slide just because. That soulful look on her face is not for her; it''s for <i>us</i>. Wonderful.</td>', 'The initial feeling here is that I was looking at a child captured, hidden somewhere, a child yearning to get out. But the more I looked, the more I realized that the child is free, and the almost mournful face is the expression that she wears looking in at us, wishing all of us adults, walled in behind our jobs and our fears and our perceptions, walled in by ourselves, could see animals in the clouds again, or run just to run, or slide down a slide just because. That soulful look on her face is not for her; it''s for us. Wonderful.', '2007-11-26 09:07:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4269403, 611770, 76103, '<td valign="top">I think the fact that it''s slighty disturbing makes it... art. After all, art doesn''t need to be nice and pretty and happy all the time. It just needs to make you feel something.<br/> <br/>But I don''t think it''s disturbing at all. You know that no harm was done to the baby! I think it gives a sense of security, just like the name. I love it. Had I had time to see it during the challenge it would''ve gotten an 8, 9 had more editing been done. I love this.</td>', 'I think the fact that it''s slighty disturbing makes it... art. After all, art doesn''t need to be nice and pretty and happy all the time. It just needs to make you feel something. But I don''t think it''s disturbing at all. You know that no harm was done to the baby! I think it gives a sense of security, just like the name. I love it. Had I had time to see it during the challenge it would''ve gotten an 8, 9 had more editing been done. I love this.', '2007-11-26 10:15:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4269482, 610917, 44877, '<td valign="top">Cool photo, Jon. I think these would be amazing apartments. There''s a lot of that kind of thing happening in the inner city here, too. Rather than letting buildings crumble, make them into something else. <br/> <br/>Lovely choice of tones for this image.</td>', 'Cool photo, Jon. I think these would be amazing apartments. There''s a lot of that kind of thing happening in the inner city here, too. Rather than letting buildings crumble, make them into something else.  Lovely choice of tones for this image.', '2007-11-26 11:03:24.000000', NULL, 0),
