(4296321, 611770, 70369, '<td valign="top">I''m confused.. This type of shot is huge right now with many many many new parents, including myself.. We tried to get this shot with my son, but he wasn''t having it.. He kept moving, so it didn''t work out.. I''ve never seen a comment like the ones you got regarding it being disturbing especially when talking about an innocent sweet picture of a baby.. Is it because it''s squished together?? Unless they know a different way to make babys, this is how they form in the womb.. It''s actually a comforting feeling for them to be held tightly together.. At least, for the baby in my tummy, I''m sure this is almost an exact immulation of the position he''s in right this very second.. Wait, I take that back, the baby in the picture actually has more room..lol<br/> <br/>Beautiful shot and I can''t wait for my son to be born so I can try again and get this myself !!!</td>', 'I''m confused.. This type of shot is huge right now with many many many new parents, including myself.. We tried to get this shot with my son, but he wasn''t having it.. He kept moving, so it didn''t work out.. I''ve never seen a comment like the ones you got regarding it being disturbing especially when talking about an innocent sweet picture of a baby.. Is it because it''s squished together?? Unless they know a different way to make babys, this is how they form in the womb.. It''s actually a comforting feeling for them to be held tightly together.. At least, for the baby in my tummy, I''m sure this is almost an exact immulation of the position he''s in right this very second.. Wait, I take that back, the baby in the picture actually has more room..lol Beautiful shot and I can''t wait for my son to be born so I can try again and get this myself !!!', '2007-12-06 14:55:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4296331, 611770, 36499, '<td valign="top">I dont find this disturbing inthe least! This photo makes me think of a baby still in the womb and I like the blue tones better than the sepia. Had I seen this during voting i wouldve given it a 10 hands down! Very thoughtful and creative photo.<br/>~~Cher~~</td>', 'I dont find this disturbing inthe least! This photo makes me think of a baby still in the womb and I like the blue tones better than the sepia. Had I seen this during voting i wouldve given it a 10 hands down! Very thoughtful and creative photo.~~Cher~~', '2007-12-06 14:58:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4296919, 609377, 48228, '<td valign="top">Stunning composion, and I love the blue tones so very much.....</td>', 'Stunning composion, and I love the blue tones so very much.....', '2007-12-06 18:18:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(4297185, 611764, 50641, '<td valign="top">What I like best about this are what some might call ''blown'' highlights (I say dramatic) and the silly face on the door. Were it mine, I might have used selective color to pull down the blacks a little. Try ''save for web'' next time, it may help with image quality.  And no matter how long you stay here, be yourself.</td>', 'What I like best about this are what some might call ''blown'' highlights (I say dramatic) and the silly face on the door. Were it mine, I might have used selective color to pull down the blacks a little. Try ''save for web'' next time, it may help with image quality.  And no matter how long you stay here, be yourself.', '2007-12-06 19:51:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(4297756, 611600, 60862, '<td valign="top">5.8?!?  Sorry I didn''t vote on this - I would''ve given it an 8.  I like the triangle of her shoulders to the top of her head, the unblinking stare, the half-visible face.  Just terrific work, David!</td>', '5.8?!?  Sorry I didn''t vote on this - I would''ve given it an 8.  I like the triangle of her shoulders to the top of her head, the unblinking stare, the half-visible face.  Just terrific work, David!', '2007-12-06 23:34:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4298001, 610315, 31637, '<td valign="top">This place looks very inviting. I like it. The photo seems a bit harsh in some spots. Looks like the processing to me. Try to leave this alone except for some dodge/burn. Boost your ISO to 500-1000 or so to avoid going to a slow shutter. Then take shutter and set to about 1/80 sec. You should have ribbon winning results.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-12-07 00:44:40.</i></td>', 'This place looks very inviting. I like it. The photo seems a bit harsh in some spots. Looks like the processing to me. Try to leave this alone except for some dodge/burn. Boost your ISO to 500-1000 or so to avoid going to a slow shutter. Then take shutter and set to about 1/80 sec. You should have ribbon winning results.', '2007-12-07 00:44:19.000000', '2007-12-07 00:44:40.000000', 0),
